{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-competitions
  The /pages/competitions hub - browsable directory of real Aussie kid
  comps, filterable by age, state, field, cost, format. Built per
  ../theinmag-docs/competitions-page-build-spec.md.

  Architecture:
    1. Three-button entry choice (art / writing / everything)
    2. Static-stage scroll zone - 100vh on desktop with the comp list
       scrolling INTERNALLY in the 2/3 column, so the page itself
       doesn't move while the user browses. Mobile collapses to natural
       page scroll, featured tile sits between buttons and list.
    3. Filter bar (sticky to top of stage on desktop; collapses to a
       drawer on mobile). Search + category + age + state. Cost and
       format were removed 2026-08-16; format's real content moved onto
       the tile as the entry note.
    4. "Missed a comp?" - in the filter bar on desktop, a stamp card
       below the stage on phone. Opens the adult-only suggest lightbox,
       which posts through Shopify's native contact form.
    5. Footer transition line.

  Data architecture: Option C (JSON in /assets/) - data lives in
  ../theinmag-docs/competitions-database.csv, gets converted by
  ../theinmag-docs/_tools/build-competitions-data.py into the parallel-array Liquid
  snippet `theinmag-competitions-data`. Migration path to Option A
  (Shopify metaobjects) is documented in the spec.

  Spotlight: admin-curated. Pool is the three competitions curated in
  the build script's SPOTLIGHT_ORDER (first = the pinned top pick,
  currently Banabae). Does NOT auto-rotate: the top pick holds until a
  visitor taps the manual prev/next arrows (crossfade between cards).

  Static-stage technique: section 2 of the stage uses an internal
  scroll container on desktop (overflow-y: auto on .theinmag-comps__list
  with scroll-snap-type: y mandatory). The bg image lives at section
  level so it's stable regardless of scroll depth. On mobile the list
  flows naturally and the bg moves with the page (sticky/fixed bg in
  transformed ancestors is unreliable on iOS Safari, so we don't use it).

  Kid characters: random-of-three pattern (per pattern library s4.4).
  Characters live in the suggest-comp modal only - shown when modal
  opens, with a slight wobble animation. Confirmed with Ryan: no
  characters elsewhere on this page.

  Data conventions:
    - Tile state: live-now / opens-in / closed / soon (TBC dates)
    - Closed tiles still render but at the bottom under a separator and
      with reduced opacity; good for SEO and "see last year's winners"
      energy per spec.
    - Tile click target: full <a> wrapper opens website in new tab.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Bring in the parallel-array data block. We use `include` (not
  `render`) on purpose: render creates a new variable scope, so the
  comp_* arrays defined inside wouldn't be visible here. include keeps
  them in this section's scope. The snippet is auto-generated; do not
  edit by hand.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- include 'theinmag-competitions-data' -%}

{%- liquid
  assign comp_size = comp_ids.size

  assign bg_pool_str = section.settings.bg_filename_1
  assign bg_pool_str = bg_pool_str | append: '|' | append: section.settings.bg_filename_2
  assign bg_pool_str = bg_pool_str | append: '|' | append: section.settings.bg_filename_3
  assign bg_pool = bg_pool_str | split: '|'
  assign day_index = 'now' | date: '%j' | times: 1 | modulo: bg_pool.size
  assign bg_filename = bg_pool[day_index]
  assign bg_url = bg_filename | asset_url

  comment
    Freshness date: prefer comp_data_updated (emitted by the build script from
    the most recent "Last verified" date in the CSV, so Compton's weekly pass
    moves it automatically). Falls back to the manual section setting.
  endcomment
  assign last_updated = comp_data_updated | default: section.settings.last_updated | default: 'May 2026'

  comment
    Character pool: pulls from the sitewide /assets/character-1.png ..
    character-N.png pool (same files the homepage uses). We emit all N
    URLs as data attributes on the section root; JS picks 4 random ones
    at runtime (one per choice tile + one when the suggest-comp modal
    opens). Pure JS-driven random per visit per Ryan's spec - not
    daily-stable. Schema default: count 100 (generous upper bound;
    JS retries on 404 so missing indices self-heal). Drop new PNGs in
    /assets/ - no count edit needed unless you cross 100.
  endcomment
  assign character_count = section.settings.character_count | default: 53
  assign character_prefix = section.settings.character_prefix | default: 'character-'
  assign character_ext = section.settings.character_ext | default: '.png'
  capture character_attrs
    for i in (1..character_count)
      assign char_filename = character_prefix | append: i | append: character_ext
      assign char_url = char_filename | asset_url
      echo ' data-character-'
      echo i
      echo '="'
      echo char_url
      echo '"'
    endfor
  endcapture

  assign tagline_text = section.settings.tagline_text | default: 'real competitions. for real aussie kids. dive in.'
  assign list_question = section.settings.list_question | default: 'what competitions are open right now?'

  assign canonical_url = request.origin | append: page.url
  if page.url == blank
    assign canonical_url = request.origin | append: '/pages/competitions'
  endif
-%}

<section
  class="theinmag-comps"
  data-theinmag-comps
  data-choice-state="choosing"
  data-comp-count="{{ comp_size }}"
  aria-labelledby="theinmag-comps-h1"
  style="--comps-bg: url('{{ bg_url }}');"
  {{ character_attrs }}
>

  {%- comment -%} ============================================================
       Choice gate - the quiz screen. Three portrait tiles fill the
       viewport. Visible only while data-choice-state="choosing".
       After a choice is made, this section animates out and the stage
       reveals. Each tile gets a random kid character (top on desktop,
       alternating L/R on mobile horizontal layout).
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
  <header class="theinmag-comps__choice">
    <div class="theinmag-comps__choice-inner">
      {%- comment -%} H1 + intro are visually-hidden but indexable. Heavy SEO lift here -
        the visible page is intentionally minimal (tagline + 3 tiles), but the H1 + intro
        contain the keywords parents actually search for. Established pattern, no SEO penalty. {%- endcomment -%}
      <h1 id="theinmag-comps-h1" class="visually-hidden">Australian kids' competitions to enter in 2026</h1>
      <p class="visually-hidden">A free directory of {{ comp_size }} real Australian competitions for kids in 2026 - art competitions, writing competitions, photography and film competitions, STEM and maths competitions, performance and music competitions, and social good competitions. Filter by age (4-6, 7-9, 10-12, 13-16), state (NSW, VIC, QLD, WA, SA, TAS, NT, ACT, national), entry cost (free, paid, paid-optional) and format (online, postal, school-entry, individual, team). Updated monthly by theINmag, Australia's magazine made by kids for kids.</p>
      <p class="theinmag-comps__tagline">{{ tagline_text }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        DOM ORDER IS THE MOBILE ORDER: everything, writing, art.
        Ryan's call 2026-08-12 - on phone the "everything" tile leads,
        on desktop it stays in the middle. Mobile is the fragile,
        majority-real-traffic view, so mobile gets the natural DOM order
        (tab order and screen-reader order match what is on screen) and
        desktop takes the CSS `order` override below instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="theinmag-comps__choice-grid" role="group" aria-label="Pick a competition category">
        <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn theinmag-comps__choice-btn--all" data-choice="all">
          <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-character" data-choice-character aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-stack">
            <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-label">everything</span>
            <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-sub">show me all of them</span>
          </span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn theinmag-comps__choice-btn--writing" data-choice="writing">
          <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-character" data-choice-character aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-stack">
            <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-label">writing</span>
            <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-sub">writing · poetry · reading · spelling</span>
          </span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn theinmag-comps__choice-btn--art" data-choice="art">
          <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-character" data-choice-character aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-stack">
            <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-label">art</span>
            <span class="theinmag-comps__choice-btn-sub">art · photo · film · dance · music</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%} ============================================================
       Section 2+3 - The static stage (100vh single screen on desktop)
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="theinmag-comps__stage">

    <div class="theinmag-comps__filter-bar" data-filter-bar>
      <label class="theinmag-comps__search-wrap">
        <span class="visually-hidden">Search</span>
        <input
          type="search"
          class="theinmag-comps__search"
          data-comps-search
          placeholder="search comps"
          autocomplete="off"
        >
      </label>

      <button
        type="button"
        class="theinmag-comps__filter-toggle"
        data-filter-toggle
        aria-expanded="false"
      >
        filters
      </button>

      {%- comment -%}
        Missed-a-comp. ONE copy now, at every width. It sits here in the DOM,
        immediately after the filters toggle, because on a phone the toggle and
        this button are a pair on the same row and nothing may come between
        them: when the drawer opens, [data-filter-group] takes a full-width
        line, so anything after it gets pushed down a row. Desktop wants it last
        instead, which is a `order: 3` in the CSS, not a second copy in the
        markup. The old separate phone card below the stage is gone: two entry
        points to one modal on a short screen is clutter, and two copies of a
        control is exactly what produced the dead-button bug.
        Sits OUTSIDE [data-filter-group] on purpose: the group is the mobile
        filter drawer, and this is not a filter.
        Two labels, one per breakpoint. Beside `filters` the button has no
        heading above it, so it has to say what it does on its own.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="theinmag-comps__missed">
        <p class="theinmag-comps__missed-copy">missed a comp?</p>
        <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__missed-btn" data-open-suggest>
          <span class="theinmag-comps__missed-btn-long">suggest a comp</span><span class="theinmag-comps__missed-btn-short">suggest one</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="theinmag-comps__filter-group" data-filter-group>
        <select class="theinmag-comps__select" data-filter="category" aria-label="Category">
          <option value="all">all categories</option>
          <option value="art">art</option>
          <option value="writing">writing</option>
          <option value="photofilm">photo &amp; film</option>
          <option value="stem">stem &amp; maths</option>
          <option value="performance">performance &amp; music</option>
          <option value="social-good">social good</option>
        </select>

        <select class="theinmag-comps__select" data-filter="age" aria-label="Age">
          <option value="all">all ages</option>
          <option value="ages-4-6">4-6</option>
          <option value="ages-7-9">7-9</option>
          <option value="ages-10-12">10-12</option>
          <option value="ages-13-16">13-16</option>
        </select>

        <select class="theinmag-comps__select" data-filter="state" aria-label="State">
          <option value="all">any state</option>
          <option value="national">national</option>
          <option value="nsw">nsw</option>
          <option value="vic">vic</option>
          <option value="qld">qld</option>
          <option value="wa">wa</option>
          <option value="sa">sa</option>
          <option value="tas">tas</option>
          <option value="nt">nt</option>
          <option value="act">act</option>
        </select>

        {%- comment -%}
          Cost and format dropdowns were removed 2026-08-16 (Ryan's call, data
          checked by Compton). Cost narrowed almost nothing (46 of 60 comps are
          free) and is printed on every tile anyway. Format was the only surface
          for school-entry and postal, so that detail moved ONTO the tile as the
          entry note rather than being dropped - see comp_entry_notes below.
          The tags themselves are untouched in the data, so either filter can be
          restored by re-adding its select.
        {%- endcomment -%}

        <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__clear" data-clear-filters>clear</button>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="theinmag-comps__grid">

      {%- comment -%} ----- Left column: chronological list ----- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="theinmag-comps__list-wrap">
        {%- comment -%} H2 is visually-hidden but kept for AEO ("H2 as question" rule per CLAUDE.md). {%- endcomment -%}
        <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="theinmag-comps-question">{{ list_question }}</h2>
        <div class="theinmag-comps__list" data-comps-list tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="theinmag-comps-question">

          {%- comment -%}
            State group headings. Hidden until a real state is picked in the
            filter bar, at which point the JS sets the flex `order` on every
            tile so the state's own comps sit under "in <state>" and the
            national ones sit below under "open to kids everywhere". DOM
            position here is irrelevant (order does the placing); they live at
            the top of the list so the no-JS reading order still makes sense.
            Each one stays hidden when its group has nothing in it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <h3 class="theinmag-comps__group-heading" data-group-heading="local" hidden></h3>
          <h3 class="theinmag-comps__group-heading" data-group-heading="everywhere" hidden>open to kids everywhere</h3>

          {%- comment -%} ---------- Live / opening / TBC tiles, top stack ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for id in comp_ids -%}
            {%- assign idx = forloop.index0 -%}
            {%- assign tile_state = comp_tile_states[idx] -%}
            {%- if tile_state == 'annual-again' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

            {%- assign cat_slug = comp_category_slugs[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_name = comp_names[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_pitch = comp_pitches[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_letter = comp_letters[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_close = comp_closing_dates[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_where = comp_wheres[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_cost = comp_costs[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_format = comp_formats_raw[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_when = comp_when_text[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_url = comp_websites[idx] -%}
            {%- if comp_url == blank -%}{%- assign comp_url = '#' -%}{%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              id="comp-<id>" makes every tile deep-linkable:
              /pages/competitions#comp-nunga-kids opens the page scrolled to
              that comp (newsletter, ads, Instagram). Deliberately invisible -
              no chrome on the tile. The JS at the foot of the section does the
              landing, because the stage starts hidden behind the choice gate
              and the list scrolls internally.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <a
              class="theinmag-comps__tile theinmag-comps__tile--{{ cat_slug }}"
              id="comp-{{ id }}"
              href="{{ comp_url }}"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-tile-id="{{ id }}"
              data-tags="{{ comp_tags[idx] }}"
              data-search="{{ comp_search_blobs[idx] | escape }}"
              data-state="{{ tile_state }}"
            >
              <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-cover" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- assign comp_logo = comp_logos[idx] -%}
                {%- if comp_logo != blank -%}
                  <img class="theinmag-comps__tile-logo" src="{{ comp_logo | asset_url }}" alt="{{ comp_name | escape }} logo" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120">
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-letter">{{ comp_letter }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-body">
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-chip">{{ comp_categories[idx] | downcase }}</span>
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-title">{{ comp_name }}</span>
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-pitch">{{ comp_pitch }}</span>
                {%- comment -%}
                  Entry note sits between cost and where:
                  CLOSES 2026-09-11 · FREE · SCHOOL ENTRY ONLY · NATIONAL
                  Only the awkward cases carry one (school entry only, postal
                  entry); an ordinary online entry needs no warning, so 38 of
                  the 60 render nothing here. This is the surface that replaced
                  the removed format filter. Note the generated array drops its
                  trailing blanks on split, so a high index reads nil, which is
                  blank, which is exactly what we want.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign comp_note = comp_entry_notes[idx] -%}
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta">
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_meta_lines[idx] }}</span>
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_cost }}</span>
                  {%- if comp_note != blank -%}
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item--note">{{ comp_note }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_where }}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-state theinmag-comps__tile-state--{{ tile_state }}">
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__dot"></span> {{ comp_state_labels[idx] }}
                </span>
              </span>
              <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-cta" aria-hidden="true">enter <span class="theinmag-comps__arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
            </a>
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- comment -%} ---------- Annual comps whose 2026 window has passed, bottom stack ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign states_joined = comp_tile_states | join: ',' -%}
          {%- if states_joined contains 'annual-again' -%}
            <h3 class="theinmag-comps__closed-heading" data-closed-heading>already run this year (back next time)</h3>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- for id in comp_ids -%}
            {%- assign idx = forloop.index0 -%}
            {%- assign tile_state = comp_tile_states[idx] -%}
            {%- if tile_state != 'annual-again' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

            {%- assign cat_slug = comp_category_slugs[idx] -%}
            {%- assign comp_url = comp_websites[idx] -%}
            {%- if comp_url == blank -%}{%- assign comp_url = '#' -%}{%- endif -%}

            <a
              class="theinmag-comps__tile theinmag-comps__tile--{{ cat_slug }} theinmag-comps__tile--closed"
              id="comp-{{ id }}"
              href="{{ comp_url }}"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-tile-id="{{ id }}"
              data-tags="{{ comp_tags[idx] }}"
              data-search="{{ comp_search_blobs[idx] | escape }}"
              data-state="{{ tile_state }}"
            >
              <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-cover" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- assign closed_logo = comp_logos[idx] -%}
                {%- if closed_logo != blank -%}
                  <img class="theinmag-comps__tile-logo" src="{{ closed_logo | asset_url }}" alt="{{ comp_names[idx] | escape }} logo" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120">
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-letter">{{ comp_letters[idx] }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-body">
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-chip">{{ comp_categories[idx] | downcase }}</span>
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-title">{{ comp_names[idx] }}</span>
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-pitch">{{ comp_pitches[idx] }}</span>
                {%- assign closed_note = comp_entry_notes[idx] -%}
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta">
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_meta_lines[idx] }}</span>
                  {%- if closed_note != blank -%}
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item--note">{{ closed_note }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_wheres[idx] }}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-state theinmag-comps__tile-state--{{ tile_state }}"><span class="theinmag-comps__dot"></span> {{ comp_state_labels[idx] }}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-cta" aria-hidden="true">view <span class="theinmag-comps__arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
            </a>
          {%- endfor -%}

          <p class="theinmag-comps__list-empty" data-list-empty hidden>nothing matches that combo. try clearing a filter.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ----- Right column: top-pick rotation + missed-card stack ----- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="theinmag-comps__right-col">
        <aside class="theinmag-comps__featured" data-featured aria-label="Top pick comp">
          <div class="theinmag-comps__featured-stack" data-featured-stack>
            {%- for spot_id in spotlight_ids -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign spot_idx = -1
                for cid in comp_ids
                  if cid == spot_id
                    assign spot_idx = forloop.index0
                    break
                  endif
                endfor
              -%}
              {%- if spot_idx >= 0 -%}
                {%- assign s_cat = comp_category_slugs[spot_idx] -%}
                {%- assign s_url = comp_websites[spot_idx] -%}
                {%- if s_url == blank -%}{%- assign s_url = '#' -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign s_state = comp_tile_states[spot_idx] -%}
                <a
                  class="theinmag-comps__featured-card theinmag-comps__featured-card--{{ s_cat }}{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
                  href="{{ s_url }}"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  data-spot-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                >
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-cover">
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-badge">top picks</span>
                    {%- assign spot_logo = comp_logos[spot_idx] -%}
                    {%- if spot_logo != blank -%}
                      <img class="theinmag-comps__featured-logo" src="{{ spot_logo | asset_url }}" alt="{{ comp_names[spot_idx] | escape }} logo" loading="lazy" width="240" height="240">
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-letter">{{ comp_letters[spot_idx] }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-body">
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-chip">{{ comp_categories[spot_idx] | downcase }}</span>
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-title">{{ comp_names[spot_idx] }}</span>
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-pitch">{{ comp_pitches[spot_idx] }}</span>
                    {%- assign spot_note = comp_entry_notes[spot_idx] -%}
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta theinmag-comps__featured-meta">
                      <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_meta_lines[spot_idx] }}</span>
                      <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_costs[spot_idx] }}</span>
                      {%- if spot_note != blank -%}
                        <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item--note">{{ spot_note }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item">{{ comp_wheres[spot_idx] }}</span>
                    </span>
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Foot row - state on the left, CTA hard right, pinned to
                      the bottom of the card. Mirrors the list tile, where the
                      "enter" button is right-aligned away from the copy.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-foot">
                      <span class="theinmag-comps__tile-state theinmag-comps__tile-state--{{ s_state }}"><span class="theinmag-comps__dot"></span> {{ comp_state_labels[spot_idx] }}</span>
                      <span class="theinmag-comps__featured-cta">enter <span class="theinmag-comps__arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}

            {%- comment -%} Manual flick-through arrows (shown by JS only when >1 top pick). {%- endcomment -%}
            <button class="theinmag-comps__featured-nav theinmag-comps__featured-nav--prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous top pick" data-featured-prev hidden>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 22 22" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="14,4 6,11 14,18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <button class="theinmag-comps__featured-nav theinmag-comps__featured-nav--next" type="button" aria-label="Next top pick" data-featured-next hidden>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 22 22" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="8,4 16,11 8,18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </aside>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
       The separate phone missed-a-comp card used to sit here, below the stage.
       Removed 2026-08-16 (Ryan: put the suggest button next to `filters`). Its
       job moved into the filter bar, so there is now exactly ONE suggest entry
       point at every width. Do not reintroduce a second copy: two copies of
       this control is what produced the dead-mobile-button bug.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} ============================================================
       Footer transition line - tiny meta below the stage
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="theinmag-comps__updated">
    checked weekly. last reviewed {{ last_updated }}.
  </p>

  {%- comment -%} ============================================================
       Suggest-a-comp modal (lightbox)
       Adult-only form per CLAUDE.md. Kid character random-of-three
       sits in the modal head and only renders once the modal opens.

       REBUILT 2026-08-16 on Shopify's native {% form 'contact' %}.
       Before this it was a bare <form> with an optional
       section.settings.suggest_form_action, and that setting was never
       filled in, so the JS caught the submit, told the person "your
       suggestion is in the queue" and threw the whole thing away -
       including an adult's name and email. Nothing was ever stored or
       sent, and Compton never received a single suggestion. The fake
       success path is deleted; there is no longer any code path that can
       claim success without a real POST.

       Where it lands: shop.email / shop.contactEmail, which is
       heyhey@theinmag.com.au (verified by Compton via the Admin API).
       No third party, no endpoint setting, no API key.

       Field naming: contact[email] and contact[body] are the two names
       Shopify treats specially. Every other contact[...] key is shown in
       the notification email under exactly that label, so the labels are
       written to be read by a human in an inbox, not decoded.

       Success state: the native form does a real POST and comes back on
       ?contact_posted=true, so the confirmation is driven off
       form.posted_successfully? and the JS reopens the modal on arrival
       - otherwise the person lands on a closed modal with no idea
       whether it worked.
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="theinmag-comps__modal" data-suggest-modal hidden>
    <div class="theinmag-comps__modal-backdrop" data-modal-close></div>
    <div class="theinmag-comps__modal-card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="comps-suggest-title">
      <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__modal-close" data-modal-close aria-label="Close">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
      </button>

      {%- comment -%}
        Modal character: JS picks one random from the sitewide pool on the
        section root when the modal opens.
        It is a <span>, not a <div>, and that is load-bearing. Dawn's
        base.css has a `div:empty { display: none }` rule, and this element
        is empty by design (the character is a background-image the JS
        sets), so as a div it was display:none on every viewport and the kid
        character in this modal has never once rendered on the live site.
        `span:empty` is not in Dawn's list. Found 2026-08-16.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="theinmag-comps__modal-character" data-comps-character aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <h3 id="comps-suggest-title" class="theinmag-comps__modal-heading">suggest a comp</h3>

      {%- form 'contact', class: 'theinmag-comps__modal-form' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          {%- comment -%} Marker the JS reads on load to reopen the modal after the redirect. {%- endcomment -%}
          <span data-suggest-posted hidden></span>
          <p class="theinmag-comps__modal-success" role="status">
            thanks! we'll take a look and add it if it checks out.
          </p>
          <button type="button" class="theinmag-comps__modal-submit" data-modal-close>close</button>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="theinmag-comps__modal-copy">{{ section.settings.modal_copy | default: 'Adults only. Send the details and we will check it before it goes on the board.' }}</p>

          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <span data-suggest-error hidden></span>
            <div class="theinmag-comps__modal-error" role="alert">
              that didn't send. {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>competition name</span>
            <input type="text" name="contact[Competition name]" required>
          </label>
          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>competition website</span>
            <input type="url" name="contact[Competition website]" required placeholder="https://">
          </label>
          <div class="theinmag-comps__modal-row">
            <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
              <span>age range</span>
              <input type="text" name="contact[Age range]" placeholder="e.g. 7-12">
            </label>
            <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
              <span>state</span>
              <select name="contact[State]">
                <option value="">pick one</option>
                <option value="national">national</option>
                <option value="nsw">nsw</option>
                <option value="vic">vic</option>
                <option value="qld">qld</option>
                <option value="wa">wa</option>
                <option value="sa">sa</option>
                <option value="tas">tas</option>
                <option value="nt">nt</option>
                <option value="act">act</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>your name (adult)</span>
            <input type="text" name="contact[name]" required>
          </label>
          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>your email (adult)</span>
            <input type="email" name="contact[email]" required>
          </label>

          {%- comment -%}
            The three optional extras. The organiser email is the one that
            earns its place: whoever suggests a comp often knows the people
            running it, and that contact is otherwise hand-scraped.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>the comp's own contact email (optional)</span>
            <input type="email" name="contact[Organiser email]" placeholder="if you know it">
          </label>
          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>their instagram or facebook (optional)</span>
            <input type="url" name="contact[Socials link]" placeholder="https://">
          </label>
          <label class="theinmag-comps__modal-field">
            <span>a couple of sentences about it (optional)</span>
            <textarea name="contact[body]" rows="3" maxlength="500"></textarea>
          </label>

          {%- comment -%}
            Honeypot. A public form wired to a real inbox gets bot traffic.
            Hidden from sight and from screen readers, skipped by tab order,
            autocomplete off. The JS blocks the submit when it is filled;
            anything that posts without running JS still arrives labelled
            "Company", so a human can spot it in one glance.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="theinmag-comps__modal-honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
            <label>
              company
              <input type="text" name="contact[Company]" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-suggest-honeypot>
            </label>
          </div>

          <input type="hidden" name="contact[Sent from]" value="competitions page - suggest a comp">

          <button type="submit" class="theinmag-comps__modal-submit">send</button>
          <p class="theinmag-comps__modal-fineprint">adults only. we use these details to check the comp, nothing else. no newsletter signup.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

{%- comment -%} ============================================================
     JSON-LD schemas - per CLAUDE.md AEO requirements.
     ItemList of every comp + BreadcrumbList + FAQPage.
============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ItemList",
  "name": "Australian kids' competitions 2026",
  "description": "{{ section.settings.tagline_text | default: 'real competitions. for real aussie kids. dive in.' | escape }}",
  "numberOfItems": {{ comp_size }},
  "itemListElement": [
    {%- for id in comp_ids -%}
      {%- assign idx = forloop.index0 -%}
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": {{ forloop.index }},
        "item": {
          "@type": "Event",
          "name": {{ comp_names[idx] | json }},
          "description": {{ comp_pitches[idx] | json }},
          "url": {{ comp_websites[idx] | json }}
          {%- if comp_closing_dates[idx] contains '-' -%}
          ,"endDate": {{ comp_closing_dates[idx] | json }}
          {%- endif -%}
          ,"location": {
            "@type": "Place",
            "name": {{ comp_wheres[idx] | json }}
          }
          ,"offers": {
            "@type": "Offer",
            "price": "{% if comp_cost_slugs[idx] == 'free' %}0{% else %}varies{% endif %}",
            "priceCurrency": "AUD"
          }
        }
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": {{ request.origin | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Competitions", "item": {{ canonical_url | json }} }
  ]
}
</script>

{%- if section.settings.faq_q1 != blank or section.settings.faq_q2 != blank -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- assign faq_pairs = '1,2,3,4,5' | split: ',' -%}
    {%- assign first_done = false -%}
    {%- for n in faq_pairs -%}
      {%- assign q_key = 'faq_q' | append: n -%}
      {%- assign a_key = 'faq_a' | append: n -%}
      {%- assign q = section.settings[q_key] -%}
      {%- assign a = section.settings[a_key] -%}
      {%- if q != blank and a != blank -%}
        {%- if first_done -%},{%- endif -%}
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": {{ q | json }},
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ a | json }} }
        }
        {%- assign first_done = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- stylesheet -%}
  /* ================================================================
     theinmag-competitions
     Multi-zone page section. Read top to bottom: choice header,
     static stage (filter bar + grid), missed-a-comp card, footer line,
     suggest modal.

     Mobile-first base styles assume phone width; @media (min-width: ...)
     promotes to tablet/desktop. Specificity-prefix pattern (s3.1) is
     applied to every mobile-override rule.
  ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-comps {
    --comps-purple-light: #E8DEEF;
    --comps-purple-dark: #5D3A7A;
    --comps-coral-light: #FBE0D6;
    --comps-coral-dark: #C9543E;
    --comps-peach-light: #FCDDB8;
    --comps-peach-dark: #D9783A;
    --comps-mint-light: #D6EAD9;
    --comps-mint-dark: #4A7C5C;
    --comps-cream: #FBF6EA;
    --comps-cream-dark: #2A1F3D;
    --comps-sky-light: #C9E5E8;
    --comps-sky-dark: #2D6878;
    --comps-yellow: #F9C23C;

    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
  }

  /* ----- Visually-hidden helper for accessible labels ----- */
  .theinmag-comps .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Choice gate - the quiz screen.
     Fills the viewport on desktop (3 portrait tiles, character at top).
     Mobile collapses to 3 stacked landscape tiles with the kid character
     alternating left / right / left down the page.

     State machine (driven by data-choice-state on the section root):
       choosing -> choice gate visible, stage hidden
       chosen   -> choice gate hidden (display: none), stage visible
     The .is-leaving class on the gate animates the fade-out before
     state flips to chosen.
  ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-comps__choice {
    position: relative;
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    background-image: var(--comps-bg);
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    /* Fill the viewport below the header. The header is roughly 80px tall
       site-wide; stage also sits at 100vh, so this matches and the page
       feels intentionally one-screen. */
    min-height: calc(100vh - 80px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 40px) clamp(14px, 3vw, 32px);
    text-align: center;
    transition: opacity 0.4s ease, transform 0.4s ease;
  }
  /* Cream wash - softer than before so the kid pattern shows through more.
     Ryan asked: "take away some of the transparency... we just want the
     background to come in a little bit further." 0.82 -> 0.55. */
  .theinmag-comps__choice::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-color: rgba(251, 246, 234, 0.55);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__choice > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

  /* Animate the gate out when a choice is made. After 350ms JS flips the
     state attribute to "chosen" and the section sets display:none. */
  .theinmag-comps[data-choice-state="chosen"] .theinmag-comps__choice {
    display: none;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__choice.is-leaving {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-24px) scale(0.98);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .theinmag-comps__choice-inner {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1320px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 36px);
  }

  /* Tagline replaces the old H1. Inter 700 (matches blog title register
     per feedback_inter_for_blog_titles), sentence-case lowercase, periods
     preserved as deliberate beats.
     Mobile: nowrap + smaller font so it fits on one line per Ryan's
     review. On phones smaller than ~360px the line may slightly overflow
     horizontally - accepted trade-off vs an awkward 2-line wrap. */
  .theinmag-comps__tagline {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(13px, 3.6vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__tagline {
      max-width: 36ch;
      white-space: normal;
      font-size: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 30px);
    }
  }

  .theinmag-comps__choice-grid {
    width: 100%;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 22px);
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__choice-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(16px, 2vw, 28px);
    }
  }

  /* Tile - portrait shape on desktop, landscape on mobile.
     Mobile: row layout, character on the side, text on the other.
     Desktop: column layout, character on top, text below. */
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn {
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: clamp(20px, 2vw, 28px);
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 0 rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.22);
    transition: transform 0.18s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), box-shadow 0.18s ease, opacity 0.4s ease;
    /* Mobile (default): landscape row */
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(110px, 38%) 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(8px, 2vw, 16px);
    padding: clamp(14px, 2.4vw, 20px);
    min-height: clamp(120px, 22vw, 160px);
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    /* Desktop: portrait tile, character on top, stack below.
       Calc keeps the tile generous but never crushes the tagline above
       or the screen frame. */
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;
      gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 22px);
      padding: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 36px) clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 28px);
      min-height: clamp(360px, 56vh, 520px);
    }
    /* Desktop keeps "everything" in the MIDDLE. DOM order is
       everything / writing / art (mobile order, see the markup note), so
       desktop reorders visually here. Only applies from 750px up. */
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--writing { order: 1; }
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--all { order: 2; }
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--art { order: 3; }
  }

  /* Mobile L/R alternation - everything on left, writing on right, art on left.
     The MIDDLE card is the reversed one to keep the zigzag, and since the
     mobile order changed to everything / writing / art, the reversed card is
     now --writing (it used to be --all when everything sat in the middle). */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--writing {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr minmax(110px, 38%);
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--writing .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-character {
      order: 2;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--writing .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-stack {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  /* Sticker tilts - subtle, restored on hover */
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--art {
    background-color: var(--comps-coral-light);
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--writing {
    background-color: var(--comps-mint-light);
    transform: rotate(0.5deg);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn--all {
    background-color: var(--comps-peach-light);
    transform: rotate(1.2deg);
  }

  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn:hover,
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    transform: scale(1.03) rotate(0deg);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 0 rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.28);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn:focus-visible {
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--comps-purple-dark), 0 8px 0 rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.28);
  }

  /* The character - large, fills most of the tile.
     Random pick from the sitewide /assets/character-1.png .. character-N.png
     pool happens in JS on page load. */
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-character {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: clamp(100px, 18vw, 130px);
    background-size: contain;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-character {
      /* Desktop: character takes the top region of the tile, sits
         comfortably above the heading + sub. */
      min-height: clamp(220px, 36vh, 360px);
      background-position: center bottom;
    }
  }

  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0 clamp(4px, 1vw, 12px);
  }

  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-label {
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(11px, 1vw, 13px);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* "Bounce off" - pressed state when a choice is made */
  .theinmag-comps__choice-btn.is-leaving {
    transform: scale(1.12) translateY(-36px);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: transform 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), opacity 0.35s ease;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Section 2 + 3 - Static stage
     Mobile + desktop both run the same static-stage pattern: stage is
     100vh tall, bg covers exactly that viewport (no stretching), and
     the list scrolls INTERNALLY. When the user reaches end of list the
     scroll bubbles up to the page so the missed-comp card + footer
     come into view. Per Ryan's review the mobile bg was visibly
     stretched + pixelated because the previous mobile stage was tall;
     locking to 100vh fixes it.
  ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-comps__stage {
    position: relative;
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    background-image: var(--comps-bg);
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    /* Mobile-first: 100vh stage as a flex column so we can flex-order
       featured (top pick) → filter bar → list. With display:contents on
       the inner .grid + .right-col wrappers below, those nested
       elements become direct flex children of the stage. */
    height: 100vh;
    max-height: 100dvh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(10px, 2vw, 18px);
    padding: clamp(14px, 3vw, 24px) clamp(12px, 3vw, 22px);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* Cream wash on top of bg so content reads cleanly. Slightly less
     opaque than before so the kid pattern shows through more, per Ryan's
     "background should come in a little bit further" direction. */
  .theinmag-comps__stage::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-color: rgba(251, 246, 234, 0.55);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__stage > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

  /* Stage hidden until a choice is made. The freshness line stays visible in
     both states (it sits at the foot of the section, just above the mag promo).
     The suggest button now lives inside the stage, so it hides with it and no
     longer needs its own rule here. */
  .theinmag-comps[data-choice-state="choosing"] .theinmag-comps__stage {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    /* Desktop: switch stage to grid so filter-bar + 2-col grid layout works */
    .theinmag-comps__stage {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;
      max-height: 1000px;
      gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 20px);
      padding: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 24px) clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 36px) clamp(20px, 2vw, 28px);
    }
  }

  /* ----- Filter bar ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__filter-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(8px, 1vw, 12px);
    padding: clamp(10px, 1.2vw, 14px);
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    border-radius: 18px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.10);
  }

  .theinmag-comps__search-wrap {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__search-wrap {
      flex: 1 1 240px;
    }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__search {
    width: 100%;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.16);
    background-color: #FFF;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    min-height: 40px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__search:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(93, 58, 122, 0.18);
  }

  /* The filters mobile drawer toggle - pill button. Hidden on desktop. */
  .theinmag-comps__filter-toggle {
    appearance: none;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--comps-purple-dark);
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    background-color: transparent;
    border-radius: 32px;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    min-height: 40px;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__filter-toggle { display: none; }
  }

  /* Filter dropdown group - hidden behind drawer on mobile */
  .theinmag-comps__filter-group {
    display: none;
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: clamp(8px, 1vw, 12px);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__filter-bar.is-open .theinmag-comps__filter-group {
    display: flex;
  }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__filter-group {
      display: flex;
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }
  }

  .theinmag-comps__select {
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    background-color: #FFF;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.16);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 9px 32px 9px 12px;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    cursor: pointer;
    min-height: 40px;
    background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, var(--comps-cream-dark) 50%),
                      linear-gradient(135deg, var(--comps-cream-dark) 50%, transparent 50%);
    background-position: calc(100% - 14px) 50%, calc(100% - 9px) 50%;
    background-size: 5px 5px;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 6px);
    min-width: 110px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .theinmag-comps__select { flex: 0 1 auto; }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__select:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
  }

  .theinmag-comps__clear {
    appearance: none;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     The grid: list (2/3) + featured (1/3) on desktop
  ================================================================ */
  /* Mobile flatten: stage becomes a flex column with featured (top
     pick) → filter bar → list. We use display:contents on the inner
     wrappers so the layout participates directly in the stage's flex
     order. Per Ryan's spec: user sees the top pick first, scrolls a
     touch to reveal filters, then the list takes over with internal
     scroll until end-of-list bubbles back to page scroll. */
  .theinmag-comps__grid {
    display: contents;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__right-col {
    display: contents;
  }

  /* Mobile order via flex: featured (1) → filter (2) → list (3) */
  .theinmag-comps__featured { order: 1; flex: 0 0 auto; max-height: 35vh; }
  .theinmag-comps__filter-bar { order: 2; }
  .theinmag-comps__list-wrap { order: 3; flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; }

  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    /* Desktop reverts to the 2-column grid: list (2/3) | right-col (1/3) */
    .theinmag-comps__grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(20px, 2vw, 32px);
      min-height: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .theinmag-comps__right-col {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 18px);
      min-height: 0;
      order: 2;
    }
    .theinmag-comps__featured { order: initial; max-height: none; }
    .theinmag-comps__filter-bar { order: initial; }
    .theinmag-comps__list-wrap { order: 1; flex: initial; }
  }

  /* ----- List wrapper + heading ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__list-wrap {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-height: 0;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__list-heading {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(10px, 1.2vw, 16px);
    padding-left: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.4vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  /* ----- The scrollable list - internal scroll on BOTH mobile + desktop ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    overflow-y: auto;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    /* When scroll reaches end, page scroll resumes - revealing missed card + footer */
    overscroll-behavior-y: auto;
    padding: 4px 6px 16px 4px;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-height: 0;
    scrollbar-width: thin;
    scrollbar-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.3) transparent;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__list::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 8px; }
  .theinmag-comps__list::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: transparent; }
  .theinmag-comps__list::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
    background: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.25);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  /* Scroll-snap on desktop only - on mobile touch-snap can feel
     finicky with the small viewport, so plain smooth scroll wins. */
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .theinmag-comps__list {
      scroll-snap-type: y mandatory;
      padding: 4px 8px 24px 4px;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-comps__list { scroll-snap-type: none; }
  }

  /* ----- Tile ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__tile {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 96px 1fr;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.08);
    scroll-snap-align: start;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
    align-items: center;
    position: relative;
  }
  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .theinmag-comps__tile {
      grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr auto;
      padding: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 20px);
    }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile:hover,
  .theinmag-comps__tile:focus-visible {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.18);
    outline: none;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile:focus-visible {
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--comps-purple-dark), 0 6px 20px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.18);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile[hidden] { display: none; }

  /* ----- Arrival highlight for a #comp-<id> deep link -----
     A share link has to say "this is the one you came for" and then get out of
     the way. Warm yellow glow, held for a beat, faded back to the tile's normal
     shadow over ~2.4s, after which the tile looks exactly like every other one.
     Colour and shadow only: nothing here changes the tile's size or position,
     so nothing shifts around it and the list scroll cannot jump.
     The tile is still genuinely focused underneath (keyboard and screen-reader
     users land on it); is-arrival-pointer below is what stops a mouse or touch
     visitor seeing a focus ring they did not ask for. */
  @keyframes theinmag-comps-arrive {
    0% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(249, 194, 60, 0.95), 0 8px 26px rgba(249, 194, 60, 0.50);
    }
    45% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(249, 194, 60, 0.90), 0 8px 26px rgba(249, 194, 60, 0.42);
    }
    100% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(249, 194, 60, 0), 0 2px 12px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.08);
    }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile.is-arrival {
    animation: theinmag-comps-arrive 2.4s ease-out 1;
  }
  /* Pointer or cold-link arrival: no focus ring. Keyboard arrivals never get
     this class, so they keep the purple ring above and stay navigable. The
     animation still wins while it runs (keyframe declarations beat normal
     author rules), so this is just the resting state underneath.
     transform:none matters as much as the shadow: the shared hover/focus rule
     lifts a tile 2px, and a tile that arrives already lifted looks stuck.
     :not(:hover) keeps the normal hover lift working the moment the visitor
     actually points at it. */
  .theinmag-comps__tile.is-arrival-pointer:focus:not(:hover),
  .theinmag-comps__tile.is-arrival-pointer:focus-visible:not(:hover) {
    outline: none;
    transform: none;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.08);
  }

  /* ----- Tile cover (letter placeholder) ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__tile-cover {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: var(--comps-purple-light);
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-letter {
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 60px);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
  }

  /* Auto-fetched logo from each comp's website. object-fit: contain so wide
     wordmark logos don't crop; small padding so the logo doesn't run hard
     against the tile-cover edges. The cover keeps its category background
     colour, and the logo sits on top - if the logo has its own background
     it just covers the colour, that's fine. */
  .theinmag-comps__tile-logo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    padding: clamp(6px, 0.8vw, 12px);
    background-color: #FFF;
  }

  /* Category-coloured covers */
  .theinmag-comps__tile--art .theinmag-comps__tile-cover { background-color: var(--comps-coral-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--art .theinmag-comps__tile-letter { color: var(--comps-coral-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__tile--writing .theinmag-comps__tile-cover { background-color: var(--comps-mint-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--writing .theinmag-comps__tile-letter { color: var(--comps-mint-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__tile--photofilm .theinmag-comps__tile-cover { background-color: var(--comps-sky-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--photofilm .theinmag-comps__tile-letter { color: var(--comps-sky-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__tile--stem .theinmag-comps__tile-cover { background-color: var(--comps-purple-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--stem .theinmag-comps__tile-letter { color: var(--comps-purple-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__tile--performance .theinmag-comps__tile-cover { background-color: var(--comps-peach-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--performance .theinmag-comps__tile-letter { color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__tile--social-good .theinmag-comps__tile-cover { background-color: #F2EBD8; }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--social-good .theinmag-comps__tile-letter { color: var(--comps-cream-dark); }

  /* ----- Tile body ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__tile-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-chip {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    opacity: 0.78;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--art .theinmag-comps__tile-chip { color: var(--comps-coral-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--writing .theinmag-comps__tile-chip { color: var(--comps-mint-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--photofilm .theinmag-comps__tile-chip { color: var(--comps-sky-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--performance .theinmag-comps__tile-chip { color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__tile-title {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.5vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-pitch {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.8;
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* The row's dimming is done with a colour alpha, NOT opacity. Opacity on
     the row would create a group that no child could climb out of, and the
     entry note below has to sit at full strength inside this row. Visually
     identical to the old `opacity: 0.62` for every other item. */
  .theinmag-comps__tile-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 10px;
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.62);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: ' \00B7';
    margin-left: 6px;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  /* Entry note - "school entry only" / "postal entry". Deliberately NOT a
     badge and not a colour: school entry is not a bad thing, it is just the
     thing a parent needs to know before a kid gets invested. Same row, same
     size, full-strength ink and a heavier weight, so the eye stops on it
     without anything looking like an alarm. Its separator drops back to the
     row's dimmed ink so the rhythm of the dots stays even. */
  .theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item--note {
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-meta-item--note:not(:last-child)::after {
    color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.62);
  }

  .theinmag-comps__tile-state {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__dot {
    width: 8px; height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--live-now { color: var(--comps-mint-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--live-now .theinmag-comps__dot { background-color: var(--comps-mint-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--opens-soon { color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--opens-soon .theinmag-comps__dot { background-color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--later { color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--later .theinmag-comps__dot { background-color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--tbc { color: var(--comps-purple-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--tbc .theinmag-comps__dot { background-color: var(--comps-purple-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--annual-again { color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.55); }
  .theinmag-comps__tile-state--annual-again .theinmag-comps__dot { background-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.45); }

  /* ----- Tile CTA ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__tile-cta {
    display: none;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    background-color: var(--comps-yellow);
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    border-radius: 32px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    /* Bumped 14px -> 17px: Post Regular reads small at uppercase, the
       "enter" CTA was hard to read. Applies to every comp tile sitewide. */
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #D4A02E;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
    align-self: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .theinmag-comps__tile-cta { display: inline-flex; }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile:hover .theinmag-comps__tile-cta,
  .theinmag-comps__tile:focus-visible .theinmag-comps__tile-cta {
    transform: translateY(2px);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 #D4A02E;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__arrow { display: inline-block; }

  /* ----- Closed tiles - reduced opacity ----- */
  .theinmag-comps__tile--closed {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__tile--closed:hover { opacity: 0.85; }

  /* ----- State group headings -----
     Only in play when a real state is picked. 43 of the 60 comps are
     national, so a state pick now reads: the state's own comps first under
     "in <state>", the national ones below under "open to kids everywhere".
     Same small-caps register as the closed heading below, one notch stronger
     (purple, heavier, fuller opacity) because this is the primary grouping
     and the closed line is a sub-note. Placement is done with flex `order`
     in the filter JS, not DOM position. */
  .theinmag-comps__group-heading {
    /* Cream pill, not bare text: the only thing behind the list is the kid-art
       background photo, and its contrast changes with the daily image. Every
       other piece of copy on this stage sits on a cream surface, so the group
       label gets one too and stays legible on any background. align-self keeps
       the pill hugging its text inside the flex column. */
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin: clamp(14px, 1.8vw, 22px) 0 2px;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    border-radius: 999px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.10);
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__group-heading[hidden] { display: none; }

  .theinmag-comps__closed-heading {
    margin: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 32px) 0 4px;
    padding-left: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.55;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  .theinmag-comps__list-empty {
    margin: 32px 0;
    padding: 24px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.6;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Featured (right column on desktop, top of stack on mobile)
  ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-comps__featured {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-stack {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-height: 280px;
  }
  /* DESKTOP: the card sizes to its own content instead of being stretched
     to match the comps list beside it.
     Was: stack stretched (flex 1 1 auto) and each card was position:absolute
     inset:0, so the card was always as tall as the left-hand list and any
     leftover height opened a hole between the copy and the CTA. A short
     spotlight pitch made it obvious.
     Now: the stack is a 1x1 GRID and every card sits in the same cell
     (grid-area 1/1). Grid sizes the stack to the TALLEST card's content, the
     crossfade still works on opacity, and rotating top picks no longer jumps
     the layout. Leftover height falls below the "missed a comp" box, where it
     reads as ordinary whitespace next to a long list, not as a gap in a card.
     Kept to >=990px on purpose: below that the featured is height-capped
     (35vh / 30vh) and the absolute-fill behaviour is still what we want. */
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .theinmag-comps__featured {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    .theinmag-comps__featured-stack {
      display: grid;
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }

  .theinmag-comps__featured-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    border-radius: 22px;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.16);
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.4s ease;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card.is-active {
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    /* Grid-stacked: same cell, no absolute positioning, so the cards
       contribute their height to the stack. */
    .theinmag-comps__featured-card {
      position: relative;
      inset: auto;
      grid-area: 1 / 1;
    }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card:hover,
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.22);
  }

  /* Manual flick-through arrows over the top-pick cover. Sit above the
     card link (z-index) and are separate buttons, so a tap navigates the
     rotation rather than opening the competition. */
  .theinmag-comps__featured-nav {
    position: absolute;
    top: 21%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    z-index: 3;
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: none;
    background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    color: var(--comps-ink, #2A1F3D);
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(123, 79, 158, 0.3);
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-nav[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-nav--prev {
    left: 10px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-nav--next {
    right: 10px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-nav:hover,
  .theinmag-comps__featured-nav:focus-visible {
    background-color: #FFFFFF;
    outline: none;
    transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1.08);
  }

  .theinmag-comps__featured-cover {
    position: relative;
    flex: 0 0 42%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--comps-coral-light);
    min-height: 120px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    /* The card is content-sized on desktop now, so a percentage flex-basis
       has nothing to resolve against and would collapse the cover to its
       min-height. Give it a real height instead - close to the 42% it used
       to compute to in the right-hand column. */
    .theinmag-comps__featured-cover {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      height: clamp(200px, 19vw, 300px);
    }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--art .theinmag-comps__featured-cover { background-color: var(--comps-coral-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--writing .theinmag-comps__featured-cover { background-color: var(--comps-mint-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--photofilm .theinmag-comps__featured-cover { background-color: var(--comps-sky-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--stem .theinmag-comps__featured-cover { background-color: var(--comps-purple-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--performance .theinmag-comps__featured-cover { background-color: var(--comps-peach-light); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--social-good .theinmag-comps__featured-cover { background-color: #F2EBD8; }

  .theinmag-comps__featured-letter {
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-logo {
    width: clamp(120px, 16vw, 200px);
    height: clamp(120px, 16vw, 200px);
    object-fit: contain;
    padding: clamp(8px, 1vw, 14px);
    background-color: #FFF;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  /* "top pick" badge - small editorial sticker top-left of the cover.
     Cream pill with dark border, slight tilt. Deliberately understated:
     Ryan + Tam want to highlight the spotlight without it reading as
     sponsored / endorsed / paid placement. */
  .theinmag-comps__featured-badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 14px);
    left: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 14px);
    z-index: 2;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--comps-cream-dark);
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 0 rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.85);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--art .theinmag-comps__featured-letter { color: var(--comps-coral-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--writing .theinmag-comps__featured-letter { color: var(--comps-mint-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--photofilm .theinmag-comps__featured-letter { color: var(--comps-sky-dark); }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-card--performance .theinmag-comps__featured-letter { color: var(--comps-peach-dark); }

  .theinmag-comps__featured-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 22px);
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-chip {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    opacity: 0.78;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-title {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-pitch {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.82;
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 5;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* Foot row - state left, "enter" hard right, pinned to the bottom of the
     body. margin-top:auto still matters: when one top pick in the rotation is
     shorter than the tallest, grid stretches its card and this keeps the CTA
     on the same baseline across the rotation. */
  .theinmag-comps__featured-foot {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 4px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px 12px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__featured-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    background-color: var(--comps-yellow);
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    border-radius: 32px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    /* Bumped 14px -> 17px to match the list-tile "enter" CTA legibility fix. */
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #D4A02E;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Missed-a-comp card - two copies render in markup:
       --desktop: sits inside the right column under the top-pick
                  rotation. Hidden on phone widths.
       --mobile:  sits below the static stage, just above the footer.
                  Hidden on desktop.
     Both share styles. Sharp corners + offset purple shadow give it a
     stamp / sticky-note feel distinct from the rounded tile language.
     Narrower than the surrounding cards per Ryan's review.
  ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-comps__missed {
    display: flex;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  /* Phone: no heading above the button, so the long self-describing label
     takes over. "suggest one" only makes sense under "missed a comp?". */
  .theinmag-comps__missed-btn-short { display: none; }
  @media (max-width: 989px) {
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__missed-copy { display: none; }
  }
  /* From 750 the filters toggle is gone and the selects sit inline, so the
     suggest button must move to the END of the row. `order` does it with one
     copy in the markup; a second copy is what caused the dead-button bug. */
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-comps__missed {
      order: 3;
      /* Tablet widths wrap it onto its own line under the selects. Hard right
         puts it under `clear` instead of stranded on the left with the row's
         whole width empty beside it. */
      margin-left: auto;
    }
  }
  /* 990 to 1099: search + three selects + clear already fill the row, so
     rather than let it wrap into an accident, it takes a full second line
     inside the bar and reads as the card's own foot. Measured, not guessed:
     the row needs about 1040px of bar before this fits alongside. The label
     comes back here because there is room for it. */
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .theinmag-comps__missed-btn-long { display: none; }
    .theinmag-comps__missed-btn-short { display: inline; }
    .theinmag-comps__missed {
      flex: 1 1 100%;
      justify-content: flex-end;
      border-top: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.14);
      padding: 10px 2px 0;
      margin: 2px 0 0;
    }
  }
  /* 1100 up: it fits on the row, hard right and away from the controls,
     with a hairline instead of a card border - inside the filter bar, a
     bordered card would read as a card floating in a card. */
  @media (min-width: 1100px) {
    .theinmag-comps__missed {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      border-top: 0;
      border-left: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.16);
      padding: 2px 0 2px clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 18px);
      margin: 0 0 0 auto;
    }
  }
  .theinmag-comps__missed-copy {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__missed-btn {
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    background-color: var(--comps-yellow);
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    padding: 8px 18px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #D4A02E;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
    min-height: 36px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__missed-btn:hover,
  .theinmag-comps__missed-btn:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    background-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    color: #FFF;
    transform: translateY(2px);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 #4A2D62;
  }

  /* ----- Phone: the suggest button pairs with `filters` -----
     Specificity-prefix pattern (s3.1). Ryan's ask, looking at 333px: put the
     suggest button next to the filters button and make the pair look
     deliberate. Same geometry as the toggle (40px tall, 32px radius, 13px/600,
     matching padding) so they read as a set, but NEUTRAL where filters is
     purple. They must not carry equal weight: filtering is the primary action
     for someone facing 60 comps, suggesting one is rare, and two identical
     pills side by side make the eye stop and read both. Border alpha is 0.55
     rather than something lighter so the control boundary still clears WCAG
     2.2 non-text contrast against the cream bar. The yellow pill is desktop
     only, where it sits alone at the end of the row with nothing to shout
     over. */
  @media (max-width: 989px) {
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__missed-btn {
      background-color: transparent;
      color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
      border: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.55);
      box-shadow: none;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      padding: 10px 18px;
      border-radius: 32px;
      min-height: 40px;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__missed-btn:hover,
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__missed-btn:focus-visible {
      background-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
      border-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
      color: #FFF;
      transform: none;
      box-shadow: none;
    }
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Section 5 - Footer transition line
  ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-comps__updated {
    margin: 0;
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px) clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px);
    text-align: center;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Suggest-a-comp modal
  ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-comps__modal {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 9999;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal[hidden] { display: none; }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-backdrop {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.55);
    backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
    cursor: pointer;
    animation: theinmag-comps-fade 0.2s ease forwards;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-card {
    position: relative;
    background-color: var(--comps-cream);
    border-radius: 22px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    width: min(100%, 540px);
    max-height: calc(100vh - 64px);
    overflow-y: auto;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.32);
    animation: theinmag-comps-rise 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.4, 0.64, 1) forwards;
  }
  @keyframes theinmag-comps-fade { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
  @keyframes theinmag-comps-rise {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(30px) scale(0.96); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0) scale(1); }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-comps__modal-backdrop,
    .theinmag-comps__modal-card { animation: none; }
  }

  .theinmag-comps__modal-close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 14px;
    right: 14px;
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-close:hover { opacity: 1; }

  .theinmag-comps__modal-character {
    display: block;
    width: clamp(80px, 12vw, 120px);
    height: clamp(80px, 12vw, 120px);
    margin: 0 auto 14px;
    background-size: contain;
    background-position: center bottom;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-character.is-ready {
    animation: theinmag-comps-wobble 3.4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes theinmag-comps-wobble {
    0%, 100% { transform: rotate(-3deg); }
    50%      { transform: rotate(3deg); }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-comps__modal-character.is-ready { animation: none; }
  }

  .theinmag-comps__modal-heading {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-copy {
    margin: 0 auto 20px;
    max-width: 38ch;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.78;
  }

  .theinmag-comps__modal-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  /* The copy now lives INSIDE the form block, because only in there can
     Liquid see form.posted_successfully? and swap it for the confirmation.
     The flex gap already spaces it, so its own bottom margin comes off. */
  .theinmag-comps__modal-form .theinmag-comps__modal-copy {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-error {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background-color: var(--comps-coral-light);
    color: var(--comps-coral-dark);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-error ul {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  /* Honeypot: out of sight, out of the tab order, out of the a11y tree.
     Not display:none - some bots skip hidden fields but fill positioned
     ones, and a few browsers skip validation on display:none inputs. */
  .theinmag-comps__modal-honeypot {
    position: absolute;
    left: -9999px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-fineprint {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    text-transform: lowercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field input,
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field select,
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field textarea {
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.16);
    background-color: #FFF;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    min-height: 42px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field textarea {
    min-height: 80px;
    resize: vertical;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field input:focus,
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field select:focus,
  .theinmag-comps__modal-field textarea:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(93, 58, 122, 0.16);
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-submit {
    margin-top: 6px;
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    background-color: var(--comps-yellow);
    color: var(--comps-cream-dark);
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 14px;
    border-radius: 32px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 0 #D4A02E;
    min-height: 48px;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-submit:hover,
  .theinmag-comps__modal-submit:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    background-color: var(--comps-purple-dark);
    color: #FFF;
  }
  .theinmag-comps__modal-success {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--comps-mint-dark);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Mobile-specific tweaks (specificity-prefix pattern - s3.1)
  ================================================================ */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    /* Choice gate - mobile uses landscape tiles stacked vertically. */
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__choice {
      min-height: auto;
      padding: clamp(28px, 6vw, 48px) clamp(14px, 4vw, 24px);
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__choice-btn {
      transform: rotate(0deg);
    }
    /* Top-pick card on mobile - sized for 35vh cap (~270px on a 770px
       phone), ensures the user sees enough but the list still has room
       below to scroll. */
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured {
      max-height: 30vh;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-stack {
      min-height: 0;
      height: 100%;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-card {
      flex-direction: row; /* compact landscape on mobile */
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-cover {
      flex: 0 0 38%;
      min-height: 0;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-letter {
      font-size: clamp(48px, 10vw, 80px);
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-logo {
      width: clamp(70px, 16vw, 110px);
      height: clamp(70px, 16vw, 110px);
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-pitch {
      -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
      font-size: 12.5px;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__featured-cta {
      padding: 6px 12px;
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .theinmag-comps .theinmag-comps__modal-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* Reduced-motion blanket */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn,
    .theinmag-comps__tile,
    .theinmag-comps__featured-card,
    .theinmag-comps__missed-btn,
    .theinmag-comps__modal-submit { transition: none; }
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn:hover,
    .theinmag-comps__choice-btn:focus-visible { transform: none; }
    .theinmag-comps__tile:hover { transform: none; }
  }
{%- endstylesheet -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.querySelector('[data-theinmag-comps]');
    if (!root) return;

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Filter logic - search + 5 selects + 3 choice buttons all converge
       on a single applyFilters() function. Each tile carries data-tags
       (space-separated) and data-search (lowercase blob).
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    var tiles = root.querySelectorAll('.theinmag-comps__tile');
    var listEl = root.querySelector('[data-comps-list]');
    var listEmpty = root.querySelector('[data-list-empty]');
    var closedHeading = root.querySelector('[data-closed-heading]');
    var groupLocal = root.querySelector('[data-group-heading="local"]');
    var groupEverywhere = root.querySelector('[data-group-heading="everywhere"]');
    var searchInput = root.querySelector('[data-comps-search]');
    var selectCategory = root.querySelector('[data-filter="category"]');
    var selectAge = root.querySelector('[data-filter="age"]');
    var selectState = root.querySelector('[data-filter="state"]');
    /* Cost and format selects were removed 2026-08-16. Their tags are still
       on every tile, so restoring either filter is a markup-only change. */
    var filterSelects = [selectCategory, selectAge, selectState];

    /* Flex order slots used when a state is picked. The list is a flex
       column, so ordering costs nothing and the DOM stays put. */
    var ORDER_LOCAL_HEADING = 1;
    var ORDER_LOCAL_OPEN = 2;
    var ORDER_LOCAL_CLOSED = 3;
    var ORDER_EVERYWHERE_HEADING = 4;
    var ORDER_EVERYWHERE_OPEN = 5;
    var ORDER_EVERYWHERE_CLOSED = 6;
    var ORDER_EMPTY_MESSAGE = 9;

    function applyFilters() {
      var q = (searchInput.value || '').trim().toLowerCase();
      var cat = selectCategory.value;
      var age = selectAge.value;
      var st  = selectState.value;
      var visible = 0;
      var localCount = 0;
      var everywhereCount = 0;
      var closedVisible = 0;

      /* Grouped view = a real state is picked. "any state" is the default
         flat list, and "national" is already one single group, so neither
         gets headings. */
      var grouped = st !== 'all' && st !== 'national';

      tiles.forEach(function (tile) {
        var tags = (tile.getAttribute('data-tags') || '').split(/\s+/);
        var blob = tile.getAttribute('data-search') || '';
        var ok = true;
        if (q && blob.indexOf(q) === -1) ok = false;
        if (ok && cat !== 'all' && tags.indexOf(cat) === -1) ok = false;
        if (ok && age !== 'all' && tags.indexOf(age) === -1 && tags.indexOf('all-ages') === -1) ok = false;
        /* State: the tile's own state OR the national escape hatch, exactly
           the shape the age filter uses with all-ages. 43 of the 60 comps are
           tagged national only, so the old exact-match-only test emptied the
           board on a state pick (NT and ACT showed nothing at all). The
           grouping below is what keeps local comps on top rather than
           drowning them in 43 national ones. */
        if (ok && st !== 'all' && tags.indexOf(st) === -1 && tags.indexOf('national') === -1) ok = false;
        tile.hidden = !ok;

        var isClosed = tile.getAttribute('data-state') === 'annual-again';
        if (!grouped) {
          tile.style.order = '';
        } else if (ok) {
          if (tags.indexOf(st) !== -1) {
            tile.style.order = isClosed ? ORDER_LOCAL_CLOSED : ORDER_LOCAL_OPEN;
            localCount++;
          } else {
            tile.style.order = isClosed ? ORDER_EVERYWHERE_CLOSED : ORDER_EVERYWHERE_OPEN;
            everywhereCount++;
          }
        }

        if (ok) {
          visible++;
          if (isClosed) closedVisible++;
        }
      });

      if (groupLocal) {
        if (grouped) groupLocal.textContent = 'in ' + st;
        groupLocal.style.order = grouped ? ORDER_LOCAL_HEADING : '';
        groupLocal.hidden = !(grouped && localCount > 0);
      }
      if (groupEverywhere) {
        groupEverywhere.style.order = grouped ? ORDER_EVERYWHERE_HEADING : '';
        groupEverywhere.hidden = !(grouped && everywhereCount > 0);
      }
      /* The single "already run this year" separator can only sit in one
         place, so it stands down in the grouped view (each group keeps its
         own open-then-already-run order, and those tiles are dimmed and
         carry their own "opens again around March" line). Ungrouped it now
         also hides when a filter leaves no closed tiles under it. */
      if (closedHeading) {
        closedHeading.hidden = grouped || closedVisible === 0;
      }
      if (listEmpty) {
        listEmpty.style.order = grouped ? ORDER_EMPTY_MESSAGE : '';
        listEmpty.hidden = visible > 0;
      }
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Filter usage tracking. Added 2026-08-16 because we removed two
       filters on a guess: the selects wrote no URL state and fired no
       events, so GA4 and Clarity were blind to filter use and there was
       no data either way. This is also the only way a silently broken
       filter would ever surface.

       The filter NAME is in the event name on purpose. GA4 will not
       report a custom event PARAMETER until someone registers it as a
       custom dimension in admin, but event names are queryable the
       moment they arrive - the same reasoning behind stack_cta_click
       using the built-in pagePath. So "does anyone touch the state
       filter" is answerable straight away, and the value is there in
       the parameter for later if the dimensions get registered.
       Search fires WITHOUT the typed term: the count answers the
       question, and free-text a stranger typed is not ours to ship.
       Guarded and wrapped - analytics must never break the page.
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    function trackComps(eventName, value) {
      if (typeof window.gtag !== 'function') return;
      try {
        window.gtag('event', eventName, {
          filter_value: value === undefined ? '' : String(value),
          page_path: window.location.pathname
        });
      } catch (e) { /* no-op */ }
    }

    /* Debounced search */
    var searchTimer = null;
    var searchTracked = false;
    if (searchInput) {
      searchInput.addEventListener('input', function () {
        clearTimeout(searchTimer);
        searchTimer = setTimeout(function () {
          applyFilters();
          if (!searchTracked && (searchInput.value || '').trim()) {
            searchTracked = true;
            trackComps('comps_search');
          }
        }, 200);
      });
    }
    filterSelects.forEach(function (el) {
      if (!el) return;
      el.addEventListener('change', function () {
        applyFilters();
        trackComps('comps_filter_' + el.getAttribute('data-filter'), el.value);
      });
    });

    var prefersReducedMotion = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Character pool - reads data-character-1..N off the section root.
       Liquid emits these from the sitewide /assets/character-N.png pool
       (same files the homepage pool uses). Per Ryan's spec: totally
       random per visit, not daily-stable, used in 3 choice tiles + the
       suggest-comp modal.
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    function getCharacterPool() {
      var pool = [];
      // Up to 30 supported - cap protects against accidental bigger settings
      for (var i = 1; i <= 30; i++) {
        var url = root.dataset['character-' + i];
        if (url) pool.push(url);
      }
      return pool;
    }
    function pickCharacter(pool) {
      if (!pool || !pool.length) return null;
      return pool[Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length)];
    }

    /* Populate each choice tile with a DISTINCT random character on
       page load. Fisher-Yates shuffle, then take the first N. Three
       tiles always show three different characters per visit (Ryan
       caught a duplicate in review - same character on writing and
       everything tiles). Modal still draws independently from the
       full pool, so a modal pick may match a tile - that's fine. */
    function shuffleArray(arr) {
      var out = arr.slice();
      for (var i = out.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
        var j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
        var tmp = out[i]; out[i] = out[j]; out[j] = tmp;
      }
      return out;
    }

    var characterPool = getCharacterPool();
    var choiceCharacters = root.querySelectorAll('[data-choice-character]');
    var distinctPicks = shuffleArray(characterPool).slice(0, choiceCharacters.length);
    choiceCharacters.forEach(function (el, idx) {
      var url = distinctPicks[idx];
      if (url) el.style.backgroundImage = "url('" + url + "')";
    });

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Choice gate transition - on click:
         1. Set the category dropdown to match the choice
         2. Run the bounce-off animation on the picked button
         3. After 350ms, flip data-choice-state="chosen" so the gate
            section disappears and the stage reveals
         4. Scroll to top of stage
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    var choiceBtns = root.querySelectorAll('[data-choice]');
    var choiceSection = root.querySelector('.theinmag-comps__choice');

    // Scroll the page so the stage's filter bar lands JUST BELOW the
    // sticky site header. Without the headerH subtraction the filter
    // row sits behind the header and the user can't see it without
    // scrolling up - Ryan caught this in review.
    function scrollStageIntoView(behavior) {
      var headerEl = document.querySelector('.theinmag-header-section');
      var headerH = headerEl ? headerEl.offsetHeight : 0;
      var top = root.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - headerH;
      window.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, top), behavior: behavior || (prefersReducedMotion ? 'auto' : 'smooth') });
    }

    function commitChoice(category) {
      if (selectCategory) {
        selectCategory.value = (category === 'art' || category === 'writing') ? category : 'all';
        applyFilters();
      }
      root.dataset.choiceState = 'chosen';
      scrollStageIntoView();
    }

    choiceBtns.forEach(function (btn) {
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var c = btn.getAttribute('data-choice');
        if (prefersReducedMotion) {
          commitChoice(c);
        } else {
          btn.classList.add('is-leaving');
          if (choiceSection) choiceSection.classList.add('is-leaving');
          setTimeout(function () { commitChoice(c); }, 350);
        }
      });
    });

    /* Clear filters */
    var clearBtn = root.querySelector('[data-clear-filters]');
    if (clearBtn) {
      clearBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (searchInput) searchInput.value = '';
        filterSelects.forEach(function (s) {
          if (s) s.value = 'all';
        });
        applyFilters();
        trackComps('comps_filter_clear');
      });
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Deep links - /pages/competitions#comp-<id> lands on that comp.
       Every tile carries id="comp-<id>" and nothing visible on the tile
       changes. The browser's own anchor jump cannot work here for three
       reasons, so we do it ourselves:
         1. the page opens on the choice gate with the stage display:none,
            so at hash-resolution time the tile has no box to scroll to
         2. a filter (or the category the gate sets) can have the tile hidden
         3. the list scrolls INTERNALLY, so moving the page alone never
            brings a tile deep in the list into view
       Runs on load and on hashchange. An unknown hash is left alone, so a
       normal visit still starts at the choice gate.
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* Input modality, same heuristic the browser uses for :focus-visible.
       A share link opened cold has had no keydown, so it counts as a pointer
       arrival and the focus ring is suppressed in favour of the warm glow. A
       visitor who is tabbing or pressed Enter on a link keeps the ring, because
       for them it is the only thing telling them where they are. */
    var lastInputWasKeyboard = false;
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
      if (e.key === 'Tab' || e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ' || (e.key && e.key.indexOf('Arrow') === 0)) {
        lastInputWasKeyboard = true;
      }
    }, true);
    ['pointerdown', 'mousedown', 'touchstart'].forEach(function (evt) {
      document.addEventListener(evt, function () { lastInputWasKeyboard = false; }, true);
    });

    var arrivalTile = null;
    function markArrival(tile) {
      if (arrivalTile && arrivalTile !== tile) {
        arrivalTile.classList.remove('is-arrival', 'is-arrival-pointer');
      }
      arrivalTile = tile;
      tile.classList.remove('is-arrival');
      // Force a reflow so a second link to the same tile replays the glow.
      void tile.offsetWidth;
      tile.classList.add('is-arrival');
      tile.addEventListener('animationend', function handler() {
        tile.classList.remove('is-arrival');
        tile.removeEventListener('animationend', handler);
      });
      if (!lastInputWasKeyboard) {
        tile.classList.add('is-arrival-pointer');
        // Once focus moves on, the tile goes back to normal focus behaviour.
        tile.addEventListener('blur', function handler() {
          tile.classList.remove('is-arrival-pointer');
          tile.removeEventListener('blur', handler);
        });
      }
    }

    function goToHashTile() {
      var hash = window.location.hash;
      if (!hash || hash.length < 2) return false;
      var id;
      try { id = decodeURIComponent(hash.slice(1)); } catch (e) { id = hash.slice(1); }
      if (id.indexOf('comp-') !== 0) return false;
      var tile = document.getElementById(id);
      if (!tile || tile.className.indexOf('theinmag-comps__tile') === -1) return false;

      /* Clear every filter first so nothing can hide the target, then open
         the stage. A share link has to land on the comp, not on a blank
         filtered list. */
      if (searchInput) searchInput.value = '';
      filterSelects.forEach(function (s) {
        if (s) s.value = 'all';
      });
      applyFilters();
      root.dataset.choiceState = 'chosen';

      /* Two frames: the first lets the stage lay out now it is no longer
         display:none, the second gives the list real scroll geometry before
         we measure the tile inside it. Rect deltas rather than offsetTop,
         because the list's offsetParent differs between the mobile
         display:contents flatten and the desktop grid. */
      requestAnimationFrame(function () {
        requestAnimationFrame(function () {
          if (listEl) {
            var listRect = listEl.getBoundingClientRect();
            var tileRect = tile.getBoundingClientRect();
            listEl.scrollTop += (tileRect.top - listRect.top) - 8;
          }
          scrollStageIntoView('auto');
          /* Glow first, then focus, so the class is already on the tile when
             the focus styles resolve and no ring can flash in between. */
          markArrival(tile);
          if (tile.focus) {
            try { tile.focus({ preventScroll: true }); } catch (e) { /* older Safari */ }
          }
        });
      });
      return true;
    }

    goToHashTile();
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', goToHashTile);

    /* Mobile filter drawer toggle */
    var filterBar = root.querySelector('[data-filter-bar]');
    var filterToggle = root.querySelector('[data-filter-toggle]');
    if (filterBar && filterToggle) {
      filterToggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var open = !filterBar.classList.contains('is-open');
        filterBar.classList.toggle('is-open', open);
        filterToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Featured top pick - manual flick-through, crossfade. No auto-rotation:
       the top pick (Banabae) holds until a visitor taps an arrow.
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    var featuredStack = root.querySelector('[data-featured-stack]');
    if (featuredStack) {
      var featuredCards = featuredStack.querySelectorAll('.theinmag-comps__featured-card');
      var current = 0;
      var prevBtn = root.querySelector('[data-featured-prev]');
      var nextBtn = root.querySelector('[data-featured-next]');

      function show(idx) {
        if (featuredCards.length < 2) return;
        featuredCards[current].classList.remove('is-active');
        current = (idx % featuredCards.length + featuredCards.length) % featuredCards.length;
        featuredCards[current].classList.add('is-active');
      }

      // Manual flick-through only. No auto-rotation: the top pick stays put
      // until a visitor taps an arrow (Ryan's call, 2026-06-16).
      if (featuredCards.length > 1) {
        if (prevBtn) {
          prevBtn.hidden = false;
          prevBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) { e.preventDefault(); show(current - 1); });
        }
        if (nextBtn) {
          nextBtn.hidden = false;
          nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) { e.preventDefault(); show(current + 1); });
        }
      }
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Suggest-a-comp modal
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    var modal = root.querySelector('[data-suggest-modal]');
    /* querySelectorAll, not querySelector. There are two "suggest one"
       buttons (the filter-bar one on desktop, the stamp card on phone) and
       the singular version bound only the first in the DOM, which is the
       desktop one. On a phone that button is display:none, so the visible
       one had no handler at all and did nothing when tapped. Live bug,
       found and fixed 2026-08-16. */
    var openBtns = root.querySelectorAll('[data-open-suggest]');
    var closeEls = modal ? modal.querySelectorAll('[data-modal-close]') : [];
    var characterEl = modal ? modal.querySelector('[data-comps-character]') : null;
    var characterLoaded = false;

    function chooseCharacter() {
      if (!characterEl || characterLoaded) return;
      var url = pickCharacter(characterPool);
      if (!url) return;
      characterEl.style.backgroundImage = "url('" + url + "')";
      characterEl.classList.add('is-ready');
      characterLoaded = true;
    }

    /* When the modal was opened, used by the speed trap on submit. */
    var modalOpenedAt = 0;

    function openModal() {
      if (!modal) return;
      modal.hidden = false;
      modalOpenedAt = Date.now();
      document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
      chooseCharacter();
      var firstField = modal.querySelector('input:not([tabindex="-1"]), select, textarea');
      if (firstField) setTimeout(function () { firstField.focus(); }, 100);
    }
    function closeModal() {
      if (!modal) return;
      modal.hidden = true;
      document.body.style.overflow = '';
    }

    openBtns.forEach(function (btn) { btn.addEventListener('click', openModal); });
    closeEls.forEach(function (el) { el.addEventListener('click', closeModal); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
      if (e.key === 'Escape' && modal && !modal.hidden) closeModal();
    });

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
       Suggest form. This is Shopify's native contact form now, so the
       submit is a real POST to /contact and the browser navigates. There
       is deliberately NO success handler here: the confirmation is
       rendered by Liquid off form.posted_successfully? when the page
       comes back. The old code faked a success message on a form that
       had nowhere to post, which is the bug this replaced.

       All that is left client-side is spam defence and reopening the
       modal after the round trip.
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    var suggestForm = modal ? modal.querySelector('form') : null;
    if (suggestForm) {
      suggestForm.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
        var pot = suggestForm.querySelector('[data-suggest-honeypot]');
        var tooFast = modalOpenedAt && (Date.now() - modalOpenedAt) < 2000;
        if ((pot && pot.value) || tooFast) {
          e.preventDefault();
        }
      });
    }

    /* Post-submit arrival. Shopify redirects back to this page with
       ?contact_posted=true, and the page reloads on the choice gate with
       the modal closed, so without this the person sees nothing at all
       and cannot tell whether it sent. Reopen the modal on the
       confirmation, and on an error so the message is readable. Then
       strip the query param so a refresh does not replay it. */
    var postedMarker = modal ? modal.querySelector('[data-suggest-posted]') : null;
    var errorMarker = modal ? modal.querySelector('[data-suggest-error]') : null;
    if (postedMarker || errorMarker) {
      openModal();
      if (postedMarker) {
        /* Success state has no fields, so openModal's focus call found
           nothing. Put focus somewhere real. */
        var closeBtn = modal.querySelector('.theinmag-comps__modal-close');
        if (closeBtn) setTimeout(function () { closeBtn.focus(); }, 100);
      }
      if (postedMarker && window.history && window.history.replaceState) {
        try {
          window.history.replaceState({}, '', window.location.pathname + window.location.hash);
        } catch (err) { /* no-op */ }
      }
    }
  })();
</script>

